# Mutation plan for the 23 local-mode pairs of `channel_local.go`, `post_local.go` and
# `group_local.go`.
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/local-channels.plan
#
# The eleven shared read handlers are mutated by their own plans; what is new here is the twelve
# handlers that *differ* from their HTTP twins by having no user, and the app-layer branches that
# difference reaches: the system bot as the author of the archive, restore, privacy and removal
# notices, the added user as the author of the join notice, no notice at all on a move, no
# creator on a create, no requestor on an add, `DeleteBy == ""` on a post delete. Each line
# below puts a user, a gate, or a notice back where Go has none — or takes one away where Go
# has one — and `the_local_channel_writes_match_over_the_socket` compares the notice each twin
# is left with.
#
# Not planned, because they are equivalent here: a requestor equal to the added user (Go posts
# the join notice for that case too); a `force` sweep with a member who is on both teams;
# `FillInChannelProps` on a header with no `~mention`; and every parameter-name change, whose
# only wire effect is Go's translated `message` (D-092).
#
# The controls: a contiguous rename of a binding and its two uses in `local_move_channel`, and a
# true swap of the `/privacy` and `/restore` registrations, which are different paths.
#
# The valid run: **14 run, 12 caught, 2 controls survived, 0 harness faults** (2026-09-14).
